<title>USA: Medtronic introduces drug system in Europe.</title>
<headline>Medtronic introduces drug system in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medtronic Inc on Tuesday said it introduced in Europe its AlgoMed drug-infusion system designed for use by cancer patients.</p>
<p>The device allows pain-wracked cancer patients to self-administer drugs through an implant under the skin of the abdomen. The maximum dosage is one milliliter and a special mechanism prevents patients from overdosing, said Medtronic.</p>
<p>About 150,000 of the estimated two million Europeans expected to be disgnosed with cancer this year will experience chronic pain, said Medtronic.</p>
<p>Medtronic designs high-tech implantable medical devices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
